# Rapid prototyping workflow

After completing user-requested code/docs changes in this repo:

1. **Commit** immediately (concise message, why-focused).
2. Run `./scripts/stamp-build.sh` and make a tiny follow-up commit if `APP_BUILD` changed (build = `git rev-list --count HEAD`). Do **not** amend just to stamp — `APP_COMMIT` is injected at deploy time.
3. **Push** to `origin` (`main` unless told otherwise).
4. **Deploy** with `./scripts/deploy.sh` (stamps version/build/commit into the upload copy).

Toolbar `#app-meta` shows `v{APP_VERSION} · build {APP_BUILD} · {APP_COMMIT}`. Bump `APP_VERSION` in the `BUILD_META` block when shipping a meaningful feature cut.

Deploy notes:

- `scripts/deploy.sh` excludes `.tools/`, `.git/`, `.wrangler/`, `docs/`, `.cursor/`, `scripts/`.
- Use ambient `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` / `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID` when set.
- Return the live URL (`https://chata-kamyk.pages.dev/…`) when done.

Do not ask “chceš commit/deploy?” — just do it unless the user explicitly says not to.
